#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Production-grade teardown for compose/laptop deployment (Darwin + RHEL).

Mirrors scripts/common/uninstall but for the laptop/compose stack:
  - Handles both RHEL (Quadlet/systemd) and Darwin (podman-compose) platforms
  - Darwin: podman-compose down, volume rm (pgdata/pricetag-data), network rm
    (pricetag-private/pricetag-mock), secret rm if exists, rm -rf ADMIN/DEPLOY,
    daemon-reload equivalent, verify cleanup
  - RHEL: systemd Quadlet stop, vLLM network preservation, manifest verification,
    owned-path validation, daemon-reload, volume/network cleanup

Flags mirror uninstall semantics:
  --purge-volumes  remove volumes (like --purge-valkey-data; default: preserve)
  --purge-images   also rm images (praxis/maas/metering/postgres/python)
  --force / --yes  skip confirmation (required for non-interactive)
  --dry-run        print actions without executing

Idempotency: running twice must not error; missing files/volumes/networks are
already-absent. verify_managed_manifest-style drift checks prevent accidental
deletion of user-modified files. flock prevents concurrent deploy/teardown races.
vLLM network preservation mirrors uninstall:26-32 (praxis-private/praxis.network
kept when vLLM owns it).

Usage:
  scripts/laptop/teardown                          # down, keep volumes
  scripts/laptop/teardown --purge-volumes          # full wipe (volumes+nets+dirs)
  scripts/laptop/teardown --purge-volumes --purge-images --force
  scripts/laptop/teardown --dry-run --purge-volumes
  scripts/laptop/teardown --deploy-dir /tmp/test --purge-volumes --force
  sudo scripts/laptop/teardown --purge-volumes      # RHEL Quadlet path
"""

